# Splitbook Project Conventions

## Repository layout

- pnpm workspace: the Next.js app is `apps/web` (package `@splitbook/web`); every path below is relative to it. Root scripts are only `lint`, `typecheck`, `test`, `test:unit`, `test:integration`, `format`, `format:check` plus the `dev`/`build`/`start` shortcuts; run any other app script as `pnpm web <script>`.

## Tech Stack

- Next.js 16 (App Router) + TypeScript + React 19
- MUI v7 (Material UI) + Emotion — sole styling system, no Tailwind
- MongoDB + Mongoose v9 — database
- Auth.js v5 (NextAuth) — Google OAuth, JWT sessions
- SWR — client-side data fetching (used directly in components, no custom hooks layer)
- Zod v4 — request validation

## Architecture

- **API routes**: RESTful, nested under group — `/api/groups/[id]/expenses`
- **Services**: Business logic in `src/lib/services/`, never in route handlers
- **Models**: Mongoose models in `src/lib/models/`
- **Validators**: Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/`
- **Components**: Feature-scoped in `src/components/{feature}/`
- **Types**: Shared interfaces in `src/types/index.ts`
- **Path alias**: `@/*` maps to `src/*`

## Data Model Notes

- Expense uses `tag` (singular string, required) — not an array
- Group has embedded `tags` subdocument array (group-scoped tag management)
- Expenses use soft delete (`isDeleted` flag) — never hard delete
- Dates stored as UTC, displayed in user's timezone

## API Pattern

Every API route handler follows: auth check → Zod validation → service call → JSON response.
Response format: `{ data: T }` on success, `{ error: string }` on failure.

## Navbar

The navbar uses `position: "fixed"` with a 56px spacer below it in the main layout. The sidebar starts at `top: 56`. Keep these values in sync when modifying layout.
